    {
        "header": "1Introduction",
        "images": [
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2610.18461/2610.18461v1/overview_v4.png",
                "caption": "Figure 1:Overview of MFVSR.MFVSR contains 3,000 paired videos from Real-HQ, Real-LQ, and AI-generated sources, together with 953 auxiliary in-the-wild videos. It spans 16 languages and four subtitle factors, and evaluates blind and mask-guided removal through five spatial views and three complementary dimensions: Restoration Fidelity, Preservation Fidelity, and Temporal Fidelity.",
                "position": 291
            }
        ]
    },
    {
        "header": "2MFVSR Benchmark Construction",
        "images": [
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2610.18461/2610.18461v1/data_construction_v7.png",
                "caption": "Figure 2:Dataset construction and unified processing of MFVSRconsists of:(1)Multi-source collection and filtering to provide a clean video pool (Section2.1);(2)Controllable subtitle rendering to generate diverse subtitled videos with different attributes (Section2.2);(3)Preprocessing to construct paired supervision assets (Section2.3);(4)Execution routing to assign each sample to the corresponding model (Section2.4).",
                "position": 323
            },
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2610.18461/2610.18461v1/taxonomy_v3.png",
                "caption": "Figure 3:Controlled subtitle-rendering taxonomy in MFVSR.The two-level ring summarizes four independently configurable factors: Spatial Layout, Temporal Behavior, Visual Style, and Language Mode and their major options, forming 24 configuration cells. Surrounding examples are color-coded by factor to illustrate finer-grained within-cell variations.",
                "position": 349
            },
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2610.18461/2610.18461v1/benchmark_statistics_v5.png",
                "caption": "Figure 4:MFVSR demonstrates rich diversity and balanced coverage.Subtitle Statistics:(a) shows a sunburst chart of language coverage across 16 languages, five script groups, and monolingual/bilingual settings;\n(e) shows balanced distributions across spatial, temporal, visual style, and language factors, whose full factorial combination forms 24 configurations with 123-126 videos each.Video Statistics:(b) indicates diverse video resolutions across AI-Gen, Real-LQ, and Real-HQ;\n(c) presents frame-count distributions with substantial variation in video length;\n(d) shows video durations ranging from short clips to sequences longer than 30 seconds;\n(f) illustrates video content distributed across nine semantic categories;\n(g) presents a word cloud of video captions, covering diverse objects, scenes, attributes, and activities.",
                "position": 515
            }
        ]
    },
